id: pm-yjq2x0
title: Honor revoked telemetry consent across capture and identity initialization
description: "An invocation started while telemetry is enabled can finish after persisted telemetry is disabled or cleared. finishTelemetryCommand currently checks only process opt-outs and retains the old installation identity. Reproduce the public SDK sequence in isolated trackers, recheck persisted consent and identity before completion capture, and distinguish already-dispatched network requests from newly captured data."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-13T21:36:42.809Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-14T01:41:28.540Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-14T01:41:27.747Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-14T01:41:27.747Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "A deferred failed read creates no completion artifacts after persisted disable; clear then reenable cannot reuse an old active installation identity; enabled unchanged installations retain lifecycle pairs; all-source coverage and public SDK regression tests pass; Independent clear after start, error, or flush preflight cannot recreate installation identity or event queue; Process opt-outs changed during awaited consent reads suppress subsequent capture or identity initialization"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Honor persisted telemetry consent throughout an invocation lifecycle
value: Privacy-safe operational context for long-running SDK and CLI consumers
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "Revalidate process and persisted consent inside shared queue transactions for start, error, completion, and flush identity initialization; keep immediate capture writes and identity creation atomic with clear"
expected_result: "Clear or process opt-out winning a preflight race cannot authorize later identity or event recreation, while completion and clear serialize their writes and deletion"
actual_result: All 117 telemetry tests and 11 consent cases pass after seven new negative controls failed before correction; full 8840-test exact coverage and expanded npm/Bun public SDK acceptance pass; production probe yields four exact pairs and no raw rejected-source value
component: telemetry capture and installation initialization
