comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T21:36:42.809Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2757-item all-status CLI export plus telemetry-clear and consent-concurrency searches found historical consent and clear implementations but no canonical item for persisted revocation during an active invocation. This is a distinct reproduction to verify before claiming remediation."
  "2026-09-13T21:39:30.817Z","harness:codex","TDD negative control: all three isolated SDK cases reproduce queue recreation after persisted disable, clear, and clear followed by reenable. Completion now rechecks both the saved enabled flag and installation identity before any deferred start or completion capture. Already-dispatched network requests are outside this revocation boundary."
  "2026-09-13T21:51:33.238Z","harness:codex","Manual packed acceptance passed in separate npm and Bun consumer roots: installed CLI initialized, created, claimed, annotated, closed, released, and validated a temporary project. Public package SDK capture followed by telemetry clear and failed completion left no recreated event queue. npx/bunx packed smoke also passed. Linked consent regression is recorded as passed."
  "2026-09-13T22:27:00.526Z","harness:codex","Full regression passed: 8832 tests across 687 files and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. All three persisted-consent negative controls pass, as do independent npm/Bun public SDK consumers. The guard checks saved consent and installation identity at completion; requests already dispatched cannot be recalled. Hosted review and merge remain pending."
  "2026-09-14T00:10:59.192Z","harness:codex","Current-head CodeRabbit feedback reproduced a check/write race with an independent SDK clear process: the old completion recreated events after clear. Consent and identity validation now share the installation mutex with deferred-start, finish, and span writes; SDK clear acquires that same mutex. Network flush scheduling remains outside. Four consent regression scenarios pass, including the deterministic negative control; full coverage is running before closure."
  "2026-09-14T00:24:55.020Z","harness:codex","Atomic consent fix passes full regression: 687 test files and 8833 tests; exact coverage 64407 statements, 49139 branches, 13389 functions, and 61681 lines, all covered. Four revocation cases include the independent-process check/write race. ESLint, typecheck, and SDK surface parity pass with zero public API changes. Packed consumers and final static gates are running before closure."
  "2026-09-14T00:37:14.169Z","harness:codex","Fresh linked consent test execution passes all four revocation scenarios. Packed npm and Bun public SDK consumers pass, with parseable JSON stdout and privacy-safe warnings; npx/bunx smoke passes. Full 8833-test exact-coverage evidence is recorded. Local static timing limitation is recorded on the linked queue item; hosted review and merge remain pending."
  "2026-09-14T00:55:53.935Z","harness:codex","All hosted checks passed for 9f2c17f12, but current-head CodeRabbit analysis found the same preflight race in start capture, error capture, and flush identity initialization. Independent clear-process negative controls fail in all three cases: stale initial enabled snapshots allow identity recreation. Reopened canonical consent lineage; extend locked consent revalidation through identity initialization and immediate append, retaining network work outside. Also verify process opt-outs that change during an awaited consent read."
  "2026-09-14T00:59:34.582Z","harness:codex","Expanded TDD matrix: seven new negative controls failed before correction, covering clear and process opt-outs during start/error/flush preflight plus process opt-out during completion read. All 117 telemetry tests now pass, including 11 consent scenarios. Start/error transactions revalidate both consent sources, initialize identity, and append under one mutex; flush initialization uses the same guarded helper and completion rechecks process policy inside its transaction. Scheduling and network delivery remain outside. Full regression is running."
  "2026-09-14T01:15:13.829Z","harness:codex","Full extended regression passed: 8840 tests across 687 files, with 64418/64418 statements, 49154/49154 branches, 13391/13391 functions, and 61686/61686 lines covered. Exact gate remains 100/100/100/100. All 11 consent scenarios and all 117 telemetry tests pass; typecheck, ESLint, and SDK surface parity pass without public API changes. Expanded packed npm/Bun consumers and final static validation are running before closure."
  "2026-09-14T01:31:37.367Z","harness:codex","Final verification: fresh linked consent tests pass all 11 cases. Expanded packed npm/Bun consumers exercise public start, error, finish, and flush after clear and confirm disabled consent, empty identity, and no recreated events. npx/bunx smoke and dependency audit pass. Static checks pass through all ten SDK import-cost entrypoints; local CLI timings exceed unchanged limits at get 389/362ms, list 421/419ms, context 435/433ms, next 506/440ms, create 436/398ms, claim 442/415ms. Earlier unchanged-base reproduction remains recorded; hosted checks are still required. Fresh Sentry has zero critical/high issues; telemetry error rate is 1.82 percent with no missing error codes."
  "2026-09-14T01:36:52.871Z","harness:codex","Current-checkout production probe 2026-09-14T01:31:46.437Z through 01:31:47.514Z delivered four starts and four finishes with four exact backend pairs. Two invocations used accepted attribution and two used a synthetic rejected override: all four rejected-source lifecycle events carried env_override_rejected and zero payloads retained the synthetic raw value. The physical queue was zero bytes after drain. This validates the bounded probe only and does not imply historical completeness."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T21:44:39.708Z","harness:codex","Revocation is checked at completion capture. Requests already sent to a collector cannot be recalled, and storage remains best effort. Clear invalidates the previous installation identity, so enabling telemetry later cannot reactivate an old in-memory invocation. This differs from process environment opt-outs, which are still checked first."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-14T00:13:32.318Z","harness:codex",A consent check immediately before an asynchronous append is still a time-of-check/time-of-use boundary. Revoke-and-delete and check-and-write must share the same cross-process transaction. Reproduce the interleaving with an independent consumer and retain flush scheduling outside the transaction so network latency cannot hold the queue mutex.
  "2026-09-14T01:03:14.519Z","harness:codex","Audit every entrypoint sharing an identity initializer when enforcing consent: start capture, completion, error capture, and flush setup can all retain stale preflight snapshots. A cheap early check is only an optimization; the decision that authorizes identity or event writes belongs inside the shared transaction and must recheck both persisted settings and process opt-outs."
